<title>USA: Pacific Scientific Q4 shr declines.</title>
<headline>Pacific Scientific Q4 shr declines.</headline>
<dateline>NEWPORT BEACH, Calif. 1997-02-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>PACIFIC SCIENTIFIC COMPANY AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>			QUARTER ENDED	TWELVE MONTHS ENDED</p>
<p>		 12/27/96   12/29/95     12/27/96     12/29/95</p>
<p> Sales     76,081,000   72,419,000  294,779,000  284,812,000</p>
<p>COST OF SALES</p>
<p>		53,613,000   45,997,000  203,074,000  186,224,000</p>
<p>Gross Profit</p>
<p>		22,468,000   26,422,000   91,705,000   98,588,000</p>
<p> SG&amp;A	 15,615,000   15,457,000   63,569,000   59,519,000</p>
<p> R&amp;D	   3,689,000    4,620,000   15,974,000   15,750,000</p>
<p>RESTRUCTURING &amp; OTHER</p>
<p>   CHARGES	    --	     --    7,500,000	     --</p>
<p>Operating Income</p>
<p>		 3,164,000    6,345,000    4,662,000   23,319,000</p>
<p>INTEREST &amp; OTHER</p>
<p>   (Net)   (1,249,000)  (1,048,000)  (4,362,000)  (3,229,000)</p>
<p>Income before Income</p>
<p>   Taxes     1,915,000    5,297,000	300,000   20,090,000</p>
<p> INCOME TAXES  769,000    1,935,000	131,000    7,340,000</p>
<p> Net Income  1,146,000    3,362,000	169,000   12,750,000</p>
<p> Primary shr 0.09(1)	   $0.27     $0.01(1)	   $1.02</p>
<p> Avg shr    12,344,000   12,592,000   12,457,000   12,514,000</p>
<p> Diluted shr 0.09(1)	   $0.26     $0.01(1)	$1.01(2)</p>
<p> Avg shr    12,344,000   13,516,000   12,423,000   13,501,000</p>
<p>(1) Includes $0.11 and $0.80 of losses and restructuring associated with the Solium subsidiary, respectively in the fourth quarter and twelve months ended December 27, 1996.  In the same periods of 1995, the Solium losses were $0.08 and $0.14, respectively.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
